# Rust
/target/
# Cargo.lock is tracked deliberately: this package ships binaries (cargo run
# --bin api / lexer-generator / test_*), and Dockerfile.api's COPY Cargo.toml
# Cargo.lock depends on it existing in the repo for a reproducible build —
# ignoring it here meant a fresh clone's docker build failed at that COPY.

# Generated output
/generated/*
!/generated/.gitkeep

/graphs/*
!/graphs/.gitkeep

/output/*
!/output/.gitkeep

# OS / Editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/

# Logs
*.log

# Temporary files
*.tmp
*.bak